```java
Contract: if a.equals(b) then a.hashCode() == b.hashCode(). The reverse is not required.
If you override equals without hashCode, HashMap/HashSet break (equal objects land in different buckets).
public final class Member {
private final String nid;
private final String name;
public Member(String nid, String name) { this.nid = nid; this.name = name; }
@Override public boolean equals(Object o) {
if (this == o) return true;
if (!(o instanceof Member m)) return false;
return nid.equals(m.nid);
}
@Override public int hashCode() { return Objects.hash(nid); }
}
// Or simply: public record Member(String nid, String name) {}  — equals/hashCode generated
