```java
Aspect: cross-cutting module (logging, security, transactions). Advice: @Before, @After, @AfterReturning, @AfterThrowing, @Around. Pointcut: where to apply. Join point: a method execution.
Spring AOP is proxy-based: JDK dynamic proxies for interfaces, CGLIB subclasses otherwise. Internal calls (this.method()) bypass the proxy, which is why @Transactional on self-invoked methods does not work.
@Aspect @Component
public class TimingAspect {
private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(TimingAspect.class);
@Around("execution(* bd.org.pksf..service..*(..))")
public Object time(ProceedingJoinPoint pjp) throws Throwable {
long start = System.nanoTime();
try { return pjp.proceed(); }
finally { log.info("{} took {} ms", pjp.getSignature(), (System.nanoTime() - start) / 1_000_000); }
}
}
```

