@CircuitBreaker(name = "memberService", fallbackMethod = "memberFallback")
@Retry(name = "memberService")
@TimeLimiter(name = "memberService")
public CompletableFuture<MemberDto> getMember(Long id) {
return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> memberClient.get(id));
}
private CompletableFuture<MemberDto> memberFallback(Long id, Throwable t) {
return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(MemberDto.unavailable(id));
}
Circuit breaker states: CLOSED (normal) → OPEN when the failure rate exceeds the threshold (fail fast) → HALF_OPEN (trial calls) → CLOSED or OPEN.
Retry: with exponential backoff, and only for idempotent operations. Timeout: always set one. Bulkhead: limit concurrent calls so one slow dependency can't exhaust all threads.
